#       beams=$(awk -v h="$hpid" '$1!=h{for(i=1;i<=NF;i++) if($i=="beam.smp"){print;break}}' /tmp/box.ps | grep -c .)
#     then resolve each remaining BEAM by /proc/<pid>/cwd:
#       ⭐ biscuit: EVERY BRANCH MUST TERMINATE IN "measured free" OR "wait" — never in the door's own
#         judgement about whether a stranger's process looks important.
#         · cwd is a TEST worktree               -> CONTENTION, wait
#         · cwd is commonplace-serve-pin (serve) -> not contention
#         · cwd UNRECOGNISED                     -> ⛔ CONTENTION, WAIT
#         · /proc/<pid>/cwd UNREADABLE           -> ⛔ BLIND, WAIT, ask
#     ⭐ FAIL BLIND if hpid is empty; never count hermes as contention, and never assume its absence.
#     ⭐⭐ EVERY UNRESOLVED CASE FAILS TOWARD WAITING. A fallback that decides whether to take a
#       shared resource must fail safe in the direction of NOT taking it.
#   ⛔⛔ AND THE RULE THAT MATTERS MOST: A DOOR MAY NEVER KILL A `beam.smp` TO FREE THE BOX. NEVER,
#     under any protocol, fallback or otherwise. A `pkill -f` matching `mix phx.server` killed
